# Citation metadata.
#
# GitHub renders its "Cite this repository" button from this file.
#
# IMPORTANT: Zenodo does NOT read this file while .zenodo.json exists — if both
# are present the Zenodo agent uses .zenodo.json and ignores CITATION.cff
# entirely. Keep the two in step by hand, or delete .zenodo.json if you would
# rather Zenodo read this one.
#
# The `license` field below is for GitHub/other consumers. Zenodo derives the
# licence from the LICENSE file itself, so LICENSE is the single source of
# truth — make sure all three agree once the licence is confirmed.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS marked TODO must be filled in before publishing.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GroMax GUI"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "TODO-YYYY-MM-DD"

abstract: >-
  A desktop GUI for GROMACS trajectory analysis. Scans folders of simulations,
  auto-pairs replicas, runs analyses (RMSD, RMSF, radius of gyration, SASA,
  hydrogen bonds, minimum distance, 2D-RMSD, DSSP secondary structure and
  shared-basis PCA) across experimental conditions, and compares the results in
  interactive, publication-styled plots. Includes multi-chain system mapping so
  residues can be selected by biological identity rather than GROMACS' flat
  internal numbering.

